      "description": "I do not know which lower loge I photographed most. Both are spectacular, with cuerda seca work and green tiles, and decoration along the insides and front sides of the arch at their entrance. I do not know their function, but think they may have been mahfili, spots where a chanter or a group of them might reside. As usual light conditions and my equipment varied over the years.",
